I believe that you need their full name inside ALL-IN-1's Message Router
which the AA can give you if you have her address a message while you're
on the phone.  Each region seems to name people differently.  Usually its
LASTNAMEXFI@BFO where LASTNAMEX are the first 9 characters of their last
name (truncated if shorter) and FI are the first two characters of their
first name.  To get the the mail through to DEC's email gateway requires
the following address parts:

	jarviske@bfo.mts.dec.com

The "bfo.mts" are the Message Transport Service internal to DEC's Message
Router backbone and BFO is the Buffalo Office's site code.

Btw, playing phone tag with Kevin probably won't stop, even if you send
him email.  If you want something, better start the escalation process
with his manager.  We got at least 2 reps removed from our account this
way.  Now we meet weekly with our rep (both Sales and Field Service).

Good luck and post if this works (the JARVISKE may be wrong but you
can get the rest from the AA).  Post any rejection notices or mail
them to me if you have problems.

/MeV/

