Convention in the TV world (and presumably the same with monitors) is that
screen sizes in inches are diagonal across the whole glass front of the
tube, including the .5" or so all round which is not usable and usually
hidden behind the bezel.

On the other hand, screen size given in cm is the diagonal of the actual
screen image.

Steve


