	The jumpers  for this board are: W1=IRQ2, W2=IRQ3, W3=IRQ4,
W4=IRQ5, W5=IRQ7 with the top being the mouse and the bottom being the
NIC; W6 is i/o port range 300-30F (with it off 200-20F is selected); W7
and w8 on are 64k at D000, W7 off and W8 on is 64k at E000, W7 on and W8
off is 32k at D8000 and both W7 and W8 off is 32k at C8000; if you have
the standard ThinWire connection then leave jumpers W9 to W14 in place
(on the bottom) and W17 on - if you have the AUI option then move W9
to W14 to the top of their jumpers and take W17 off; W15 is for grouding
of the AUI option - if it has 9 pins then remove W15 otherwise leave it
on; finally if you want remote booting then remove W16 otherwise leave
it on.

	That should do it.  Have fun.

