||>
|>    Looking at C, BLISS, FORTRAN, and Macro32 for example, how much progress
|>   has there *really* been in "languages" since the 1960's?   There have been
|>   a lot more advances in hardware.  When I came out of tech school in the 
|>   60's, I looked forward to a day when we could soon talk to our computers.
|>   Looks like it might start soon now, but it's really about 25 years late
|>   by my expectations.
