Hi Jim

I'm using a DEC_Station 5000/33 with Ultrix V4.2A. Also we have a VMS Cluster
with VAX 6310&6410. I print from my Station with LAT to the same Laserprint
that the VMS-Queu does.
I add my LASER Printers with the /etc/lprsetup procedure. It is really easy
to do. Just take care by follows parameters:
                ct=lat        Option for lat
                ts=SERVER     Name from Terminalserver (probably UPPERCASE)
                op=PORT_1     Port Number (probably UPPERCASE)
                sh=:\         Switch on for no Banner

And be sure to configure the Terminal Server Port with LATGROUPS for 0-255.
Otherwise you can't do a connection to the printer. Also check the device on
the Ultrix Station. Mostly you have to add a new device in the /etc/rc.local
file or to change the /etc/ttys file. I preffer to do the changes in the
/etc/rc.local file :

example from my rc.local file
if [ -f /etc/lcp ] ; then
        /etc/lcp -s -h /dev/tty10 >/dev/console
        /etc/lcp -h /dev/tty09 >/dev/console
        /etc/lcp -h /dev/tty08 >/d
        /etc/lcp -h /dev/tty07 >/dev/console
        /etc/lcp -h /dev/tty06 >/d
        /etc/lcp -h /dev/tty05 >/dev/console
        /etc/lcp -h /dev/tty04 >/dev/console
fi
