braun@ann-arbor.applicon.slb.com (Matthew Braun) writes:

| Has anyone had experience with running a DECstation with both an HX
and
| PXG graphics boards installed?

I do not believe that you can run the PXG and the HX on the same system
at the same time.  At least I know that we physically disabled it from
working in the software on AXP.

The basic problem is that a design flaw in PEX (at least in my
opinion) does not provide a way to tell on a per-screen basis if
the extension is supported.  Unless there is a software based
PEX extension available for the HX head, then you are bound to
have many problems when you run 3D apps.

I have run the PXG and HX together on a OpenVMS AXP system (it shares
common source with OSF) -- without the 3D extension present, and it
appeared to work for 2D.  But we do not support that configuration.

I expect the story is the same on the DECstation 5000.

