In article <1993Aug23.203132.17198@ncsu.edu>,
                                hmn@unity.ncsu.edu (Harry Nicholos) writes:
> I have inherted a VAXstation 2000 and would like to have it boot from the
> networked cluster we have running.  How can I setup the 2000, via the
> console, to automatically boot from ESA0.

    At the three-arrow prompt, type TEST 51 and hit RETURN.  You will
be presented with a prompt that looks something like

        DUA0 ? >>>

Respond with ESA0 and hit return:

        DUA0 ? >>>ESA0

Now the boot device is set to the ethernet device ESA0.


    Note that you will still need to configure the cluster to allow your
VS2000 to be a member and boot off the boot-node.  You (or your
system manager) will need to

                $ @SYS$MANAGER:CLUSTER_CONFIG

to add your node to the cluster.  You will need to supply the ethernet
hardware address.  You can get that via TEST 50.  Look at the output
of TEST 50 and you'll see that the 2nd or 3rd line is something like

        ID 08-00-2B-02-CF-A4

The numbers following "ID" are the hardware ethernet address.

        -Ken
