>>need, i.e. just a few restores?)

You can still get DEC's implementation of BRU under VMS, it ships with the AME.
AME (Applications Migration Executive) is basically an RSX-11M (or is it M+?)
emulator which runs under VMS.

The AME was built into VMS 1 and 2, but became optional for VMS 3.  Of course,
getting BRUREAD from DECUS is probably a lot cheaper.  The AME no longer
requires compatability mode support in the hardware (I assume its emulated).

