I can't hope to answer most of these questions, but I do still admit
to once having worked for the engineering group responsible for it.

The machine is a PDP-11 and despite a lot a bad things about it, it's
pretty good PDP-11 (well, not as good as a PRO 380 ;-)

It will run POS (Professional Operating System) which is a variant
of RSX11M+, as well as VENIX.  It uses RX50 floppies (if I remember
correctly).  It will NOT run random PC software.  You may need the
monitor to be able to boot it.  I believe that if you get a cable
with a DB9 with two of the pins shorted (the cables were labeled
"console" and are the same ones used on the VS2000) you can get it
to boot using the serial line as the console.  To get software for it,
you probably need to contact your local DEC office... I long ago
got rid of all my software for it.


