<I've got yet more questions to throw into this discussion. What (in DECnet)
<is meant by a Negative acknowledgement, and why would it be sent? 

	In the DECnet NSP architecture, a NAK message is defined and it tells
the sender to immediately retransmit any unacknowledged data.
	Nothing in the specification defines any situation in which you must
send a NAK.  So you most likely will never see one, or if you do, it's done by
system dependent implementation, not by architecture.
	(the only implementation I know of is the one that can be turned on
by management command in DECnet-DOS)

	Dave.
