In article <1993Aug20.151419.3007@glv.uucp>, bounds@gulaam.glv.com (Frank Bounds) writes...
> 
>	Is VMS mostly Bliss code now? Or is there still a significant portion
>	in MACRO. How about OpenVMS/Alpha? C? Bliss? This came up in a
>	discussion and I am curious... 

The VMS exec is mostly written in VAX MACRO or MACRO-32. This is true
on Alpha as well since significant portions were ported using the MACRO
compiler, developed for Alpha. As you move away from the exec into
utilities, etc., you see other languages more. There's a lot of BLISS,
some C, and a variety of other languages as well (PASCAL and PL/I to name
a couple).

When the initial port was done to Alpha, most new code was written in
BLISS, replacing MACRO code. However, some new code was also written
in MACRO-64 (Alpha assembler). So another language was thrown into the
pot.

Nowadays, most new code is being written in C, especially on Alpha.
This will be the trend for a while. You should see more and more new C
code and less and less MACRO and BLISS over time.

