Frank,
 
OpenVMS (have to remember to be politically correct!) is written 
in quite a few languages. Large parts are written in MACRO-32, 
other components are written in "C", at least one part is written 
in PL/I (MONITOR, last time I needed to look at the source), and, 
I would not be surprised to discover that there is at least one 
part of the system which has been written in each of the major 
languages.
 
On the ALPHA, most of the code was recompiled (this includes the 
MACRO-32 code, which is run through a MACRO-32 COMPILER, which 
translates MACRO-32 into executable ALPHA instructions.
 
In a simple sense, this is the process. Obviously, there is not 
100% commonality between AXP and VAX, but, as I seem to recall, 
very little code is actually written in MACRO-64.
 
As time goes on, more and more code will probably be re-written 
in a high level language (I suspect "C"), but, given the overall 
size of the system, I suspect that much of the MACRO-32 code will 
be around for awhile.
 
