11/45 had 18 bit memory management, the 11/70 provided 22 bit memory management
and a fast peripheral to memory slots (to which DEC  connected the MASSBUS
disk/tapes).  Both had split I&D spaces.

You left out the 1979 (ish) intructuction of an 11/34.  Octal front panel
