The 11/23 and 24 had the 11/34 style memory management.

There was also a 1982 introduction of the T11 Falcon chip) standard PDP-11
core set with the exception of MARK (What no mark instruction?).  Board
marketed under 11/21?

There was a WCS option for the LSI's, but only one customer bought it
(some typesetting house)..

The numbers like 05, 15, 35 were used to designate the processor in an
integrated system.

> All the HSCxxx Storage controllers use PDP-11 processors.
> ...and elsewhere.

Only for control, the data paths were 2900 bitslices.


Most of the PDP-11 line board the standard maroon and purple colors.
The 55 and some of the integrated systems were blue and green (as
were the DEC-10 FEP 40's and some later front panel less 70's).  The 11/60 came in the low boy (VAX) style.  The 11/34 and the later unibus (24, 44) came
