	I'll hop on this one, it's one of my favorite pet peeves with
DECnet-VAX:  Yes, out-of-the-box the default retransmission timers are much 
too long.  I recommend:

1) Reduce EXEC DELAY FACTOR from 80 to 32.
	This is the primary control.  It is a multiplier (in sixteenths) 
	of the current dynamic measured round-trip-delay until timing out
	an NSP segment.

	This will make it timeout & retransmit much faster.

2) Since we'll time out faster, lets be willing to do it longer (to preserve
the typical time until link timeout.)  so 
	Raise EXEC RETRANSMIT FACTOR from 8 to 18


