>>>>> On Wed, 18 Aug 1993 01:05:31 GMT, ken@syd.dit.CSIRO.AU (Ken Yap) said:

	Ken> We've got an old MicroVax II (actually has the label
	Ken> AIStation on it).  When it powers up it goes through the
	Ken> hardware self-test and stops with the >>> prompt. At this
	Ken> point one has to type B to boot.

	Ken> I'd like it to continue by itself. Power failures at
	Ken> night, etc. Also I'd like to to boot from DUA1: instead
	Ken> of the default DUA0:.

	Ken> How, if at all, can modify the boot sequence? Please email.

There's a bulkhead in the back of the system that has a 1 character
LED display, a toggle switch, and a rotary switch. Next to the toggle
switch there are 2 circles, one with a dot or a triangle in the
circle, and one with the dot/triangle outside of the circle; you want
to flip the toggle switch so that it's next to the circle with the dot
outside, that will disable the halt button on the front of the system
and it will also cause the system to automatically reboot on a powerup
or system reset.

The boot ROM has a sniffer that will search a floppy disk, a hard
disk, a tape drive, and Ethernet (in that order) for a bootstrap
image; as long as DUA0 isn't a system disk (and DUA1 is) it should do
what you want when it boots.

/harley
