	DEC does provide one, but without official support, for the
DE200.  It also works with the DE100 and DE210.  It's available via
anonymous ftp at gatekeeper.dec.com, but I forget which directory it's
in.

	However a better bet, in my opinion, is to use NDIS with the
DIS_PKT "shim".  This provides packet driver support, but since it's on
top of NDIS it will work with any card that has NDIS support AND it will
work concurrently with other protocols (DECnet for instance).  This is
commonly available.

	See the news group comp.protocols.tcp-ip.ibmpc for lots more
info on this subject.  Especially see the FAQ, which you can find via
anonymous ftp at ftp.cac.psu.edu in pub/dos/info/tcpip.packages.

	p.s. rumor has it that DEC won't provide a native mode packet
driver for the Etherworks 3 cards.  Also, I have tried both of the
above solutions and had the best results with the latter solution, and
yes, it did work with QVTNet
 
