This has been answered some time ago, and maybe someone might be in a
position to extract the original and repost.

Briefly:
1970:   11/20, 11/15 born. Small Scale integration. 4 or 8k mem. Core.
        TTY console Papertape reader/punch typical I/O

1972 (ish) 11/45 first of the highspeed processors that begat 11/55,
        11/70 (1975). 11/45 Microcoded, SSI/MSI, memory bus, core. 11/55
        had special bipolar high speed mem. 11/70 had core initially and
        MOS later. These machines introduced Cache, Floating point
        processors, etc.

1974 (ish) 11/40, 11/35. Price same as 11/20, higher perf. Architecture
        of cpu like 11/45 without the raw power. EIS/FIS Extended and
        Floating instruction sets as options. Core then MOS. Microcoded

1974 (ish) 11/05, 11/10. Perf same as 11/20, lower price. Microcoded.
        2-board processor.

1975 (ish) LSI-11 PDP 11 implemented on 4 chips. First of the Q-bus
        machines (All others above were UNIBUS. 

1976 (ish) LSI-11/2 "Real) PDP11 on a microprocessor. Perf = 11/05,
        price much less. Qbus
1976 (ish) 11/03 Same microprocessor. Perf = 11/05, price much less.
        Qbus
1976 (ish) 11/04 Same microprocessor.Follow on to 11/05. Perf = 11/05,
        price much less.  Unibus

1977    11/60. Follow on to 11/40. Higher performance. Writable control
        store for custom instructions. Too costly, too late.

1980 (ish) 11/44. successful follow on to 11/40, 11/70. 11/70 power at
        11/40 price. Unibus

1980 (ish) 11/23. successful follow on to 11/03. F-11 chip. Perf GT 
        11/03 at lower cost. Qbus
1980 (ish) 11/24. successful follow on to 11/04. F-11 chip. Price of
        11/04 Higher perf. 


198x    11/73, 11/7?. Followons to 11/23, 11/24. J-11 chip. Similar
        cost, higher perf. Replacements for 11/44, 11/70

198x    11/83, 11/84    Higher perf versions of 11/7x. Highest perf
        PDP-11s

Generally, later model -11s with even numbers are UNIBUS machines and
        Odd numbered oned are Qbus machines.

The PDP-11 processors have also found themselves in other roles:
        -Most PDP-10/DECsystem-10 and DECsystem-20 prontend processors
        and communications processors were PDP-11/20 and /40s.
VAX11780 front end processor/console was and 11/03
VAX11750 FEP was, I think, and LSI11
LAT originally implemented on PDP-11s as comms processors.
DECSA Ethernet Term Server had PDP-11 as a heart.
All the HSCxxx Storage controllers use PDP-11 processors.
...and elsewhere.
       
[All from memory. Dates and other details may be slightly off]

Mike
