Heartbeat one major benefit, it provides feedback that the collision detect
line from the transceiver is still hooked up.  The premise under which Ethernet
operates goes to pot pretty fast if you stop being able to detect collisions.
Heartbeat blips the CD line after each transmission so the host can detect
things gone awry and stop transmitting.  Some systems also use this to verify
that the cable is plugged in at all, but this can be accomplished via other
means (like listening to ones own carrier).

-Ron


