It is quite well known, that X11R5 code is one of the most difficult examples
when concidering portability to 64bit. DEC OSF/1 AXP has well functioning and
robust X11R5 environment and libraries built in out of the box. Porting has been
done by Digital. I have personally ported, tested and benchmarked several
(even huge) applications on DEC OSF/1 AXPm and as conclusion I'd say that 
in most cases 64bit pointers aren't problem at all. Trusting to length of the 
pointer has never been good coding practise !


>	    As for third party software, DEC has started paying penalties
>	to us because the software is not arriving according to the schedule in
