||> I have a problem with DECnet on two ethernet connected machines, across
|>a routed FDDI network using Cisco routers. A data transfer seems to progress
|>normally, and then stop for a while, and begin again. When the transfer was
|>captured, the problem seems to be with retransmission timeouts. However,
|>I don't have any detailed explanation of the NSP so could anyone explain
|>what is happening below. The segments are ack'd normally until number
|>894, which takes multiple retransmits. The same happens with segment 903
|>however this time the sender (ESTCS1) waits about 6 seconds, and resends
|>from segment 903. A second sniffer has shown the ack's reaching ESTCS1
|>so what is happening here? And why does it take 6 seconds for the sender
