If the NSP Acks are really reaching the node in question, I'd make the sure
(assuming this is VMS) the line receive buffers is higher than default (say,
up them to 32 or so).  [What type of machines are involved and what are they
running?]

BTW, the problem isn't that the ACK for 894 did or didnot reach ESTCSG.  The
problem is that segment 895 did not reach ESTCS1 but ones following did.
This causes ESTCSG to retransmit the ack for the last segment it did receive
(which was 894).

