You can get around this even more by putting a local system disk in each
LAN connected by the WAN. Since every NFS node has it OS on a local
disk it is no wonder that it hasn't got this problem, and since the
VMS cluster systems all operate off of (typically) one system disk
it is no wonder that they do have this problem - on the other hand
they have considerably more free disk space due to the removal of
N-1 copies of the operating system in a cluster of N nodes.

NFS and VMSclusters are not the same thing. They are not even supposed to be
the same thing. No wonder they don't work the same. What a surprise.

--- Carl


