|>Help!! I need some help in reference to a DEC Alpha 3000/400 system
|>running openVMS 1.5. I have read in the release notes that DECNet
|>will only support one circuit on openVMS/Alpha I am being forced 
|>to have 2 ethernet cards in my system. One for local connections
|>(terminal servers) and another for internet connection (our main
|>network). Would that be 1 circuit or 2??

If your internet connection is TCP/IP based, then DECnet doesn't enter
the picture.

The problem is that AXP/VMS does not yet support routing nodes, and
end nodes are only allowed to have one active circuit. If your internet
connection is TCP/IP based, then DECnet doesn't enter the picture.

