system.  However, the hang only occurs when we have the 3800 CPU in the
system.  If we swap in the MicroVAX II CPU (and related memory) the hang
does not occur.  The symptoms of the hang are strange - it hangs so hard that
the Break key on the console and the halt button on the CPU cannot budge
it.  The only way to free it is to hit the restart button - therefore we
cannot get a dump.  When it hangs, the letter "E" is displayed on the LED
on the CPU card.  The hangs seems to occur when both of the 760 interfaces
are in use.  Data is input at a rate of either 132 Kb/sec or 264 Kb/sec and
since both interfaces are active and their data is also being written to
disk, the total bus throughput can reach a peak of 1056 Kb/sec.  This seems
high, but the MicroVAX II can keep up.  The data rates normally are only
hitting about 792 Kb/sec when the hang occurs and sometimes the rate is
