In article <jrl2.744574081@crux1.cit.cornell.edu>, jrl2@crux1.cit.cornell.edu (Jeffrey R. Luszcz) writes:
|> Well Hello,
|>   I've just picked up a DEC GIGI termial. All I have is
|> the keyboard. The keyboard has outputs for RGB output,
|> also mono, a printer, rs232 and 20mA.
|>  My questions are...
|>     what type of monitor can i hook it up to. I tried hooking
|>     it upto a vt100 with the mono input but nodice.

The recommended monitor is a Barco GD33 colour monitor. The manual
states that you can also connect to a 'typical black and white
monitor'. The specs for this mono port are 75 Ohm, sync level 0.0 to
0.1 volt, black level 0.3V +-10%, white level 1.0V +-10%. Frame rate
(interlaced) is either 60Hz or 50Hz, depending on the setting
of dip switch 1 (see below), and half that value if interlacing isn't
enabled (depending on one of the setup menu values).

The colour port has sync on green. 
|> 
|>    Also, what does the row of dip switches control??
1: down: 60Hz power
   up: 50 Hz
2: down: EIA comms
   up: 20 mA comms
3: down: default char set is US
   up: default char set is UK
4,5: both down: parity off
     4 down, 5 up: even
     4 up, 5 down: odd
6,7,8: control baud rate. all down is 110, all up is 19200,
6 & 7 down & 8 up is 300, working in straight binary progression.

As far as I can tell, all these can be over-ridden from the 
setup menus.
