In article <CB0Ftn.948@acsu.buffalo.edu>, kalisiak@cs.buffalo.edu (Chris Kalisiak) writes:

> Hmmm... I distinctly remember seeing a diagram of a cascade starting
> with a DELNI, but I don't remember what the devices were... Is it possible
> that the DEMPR (which came out before the DESPR) is the ENET-II devices
> I saw, or can you only cascade DELNI's?

A DEMPR can be connected to a DELNI if the tranceiver port on thhe DELNI does
not receive heartbeat.  An H4000 tranciever supplies heartbeat.  Most
tranceivers later than that have switchable heartbeat.  If you are using the
DELNI in a standalone mode (no tranceiver, switch closed), the DELNI supplies
heartbeat and therefore won't work with the DEMPR.  The simple solution in
this case is to open the switch and plug a loopback connector (the one supplied 
with the DEMPR or DELNI) into the tranceiver port.  This has the added benefit
of the pretty green light so you can tell when the DELNI is powered on :-).
