And clueless as well. Or he was treating you as an idiot.

Fire up sysgen and look at the parameter 'VOTES', and  if "DISK_QUORUM'
is non null, 'QDSKVOTES'. add the two, and that will tell you how many
votes that node has. Add them all up across all nodes, and the result
should be 'EXPECTED_VOTES'. In the old scheme you needed (total_votes)/2+1
to run. Hence a 2 way partition could result in the smaller partition
having 1/2 of the votes ( OK smaller isn't =, I know, ) so it would
suspend. If a small part of the cluster 'fell off', the major section
could continue, and after RECNXINTERVAL they are removed from the cluster.
If they come back with the same cluster ID ( ie they have not been re-
booted ) they are bugchecked out as the lock database has now been re-built
to remove them from the sustem, and they *CAN'T* be allowed to come in
without a complete lock re-build, re-mounting of disks etc etc.

BTW, in every cluster site I have been in, near the consoles was
D/I 14 C ...

Does anyone know the ins and outs of the quorum change? I assume it was
explained at a decus sesion at some stage.

~Paul



