> 	o  I saw a posting from 1988 where someone quoted a DEC memo which
> 	   stated that on a 3000 series system, Unibus boards connected to a
> 	   Qbus to Unibus adapter can cause such strangeness if the Unibus
> 	   board uses THIPR (transparent hardware initiated passive release).
> 	   I have looked in the book for the 760 (fairchild) and can't find
> 	   anything about it.  How can we find out if it uses THIPR?  How can
> 	   we find out if the DEC DSS11 Unibus board uses THIPR?

My first suspicion would be the CSS board, or the q-bus to unibus converter.
From memory there was also problems with some 3rd party controlers as well.
The passive release BTW is where a controler drops its NPR line when it
sees a BRx request, so as to reduce interupt latency. This could result
in NPG being driven forever in some cases...

